        {
          "id": 3757899298,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I guess I haven't gotten this far to realize it would be a problem.\n\nWhere I have been hung up is getting the newer version of WiX to match NSIS as far as the \"component install tree\".  WiX keeps forcing a single parent (i.e. Wireshark) with all components then under that (Wireshark, TShark, etc).  I like the NSIS \"look\" of having Wireshark and TShark (and presumably Stratoshark, etc) at the same tree level for the installation.",
          "author": {
            "id": 8399509,
            "username": "mmann78",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Michael Mann",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
