        {
          "id": 3756752837,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "If I interpret https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/cpp/porting/binary-compat-2015-2017 correctly, it looks like modern C++ runtime versions are backward compatible with binaries built against them but not necessarily forward compatible:\n\n> The Redistributable your app uses has a similar binary-compatibility restriction. When you mix binaries built by different supported versions of the build tools, the Redistributable version must be at least as new as the latest build tools used by any app component.",
